<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obanta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Obanta is the legendary founder of the Ijebu Kingdom in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. According to Ijebu tradition he migrated from Ile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a>, the ancestral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> city, and settled at Ijebu-Ode, which became the capital of the kingdom. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awujale">Awujale</a>, the kings of Ijebu, regard him as the ancestor of their line, and his memory is central to the town's account of its origins.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obanta.jpg" alt="Obanta" width="148" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adeola · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obanta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
